	"transcription": [
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:00,000",
				"to": "00:00:01,820"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 0,
				"to": 1820
			},
			"text": " This question comes from me."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:01,820",
				"to": "00:00:05,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 1820,
				"to": 5200
			},
			"text": " It's a new chapter from the 10th anniversary edition of What If, which is now available"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:05,200",
				"to": "00:00:06,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 5200,
				"to": 6760
			},
			"text": " online and in print."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:06,760",
				"to": "00:00:09,540"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 6760,
				"to": 9540
			},
			"text": " At the end of the laser pointer video, we constructed an array of lasers with a total"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:09,540",
				"to": "00:00:14,580"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 9540,
				"to": 14580
			},
			"text": " power of 2 x 10^24 watts, which not only lit up the moon, but violently ejected it from"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:14,580",
				"to": "00:00:15,660"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 14580,
				"to": 15660
			},
			"text": " orbit around the Earth."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:15,660",
				"to": "00:00:17,500"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 15660,
				"to": 17500
			},
			"text": " We decided that was enough power."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:17,500",
				"to": "00:00:18,540"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 17500,
				"to": 18540
			},
			"text": " But why?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:18,540",
				"to": "00:00:19,980"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 18540,
				"to": 19980
			},
			"text": " You can always make a number bigger."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:19,980",
				"to": "00:00:21,100"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 19980,
				"to": 21100
			},
			"text": " No one can stop you."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:21,100",
				"to": "00:00:22,940"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 21100,
				"to": 22940
			},
			"text": " There are infinitely many numbers."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:22,940",
				"to": "00:00:26,180"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 22940,
				"to": 26180
			},
			"text": " And I want to know, what if we tried even more power?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:26,180",
				"to": "00:00:30,420"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 26180,
				"to": 30420
			},
			"text": " A 2 x 10^24 watt laser is powerful."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:30,420",
				"to": "00:00:34,020"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 30420,
				"to": 34020
			},
			"text": " When we turned ours on, it made the moon facing surface of the Earth significantly more luminous"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:34,020",
				"to": "00:00:35,020"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 34020,
				"to": 35020
			},
			"text": " than the sun."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:35,020",
				"to": "00:00:37,100"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 35020,
				"to": 37100
			},
			"text": " That's impressive, but we can do better."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:37,100",
				"to": "00:00:40,540"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 37100,
				"to": 40540
			},
			"text": " The universe contains death rays that make our moon obliterating beam look like a handheld"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:40,540",
				"to": "00:00:41,780"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 40540,
				"to": 41780
			},
			"text": " laser pointer."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:41,780",
				"to": "00:00:42,780"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 41780,
				"to": 42780
			},
			"text": " Gamma ray bursts."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:42,780",
				"to": "00:00:47,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 42780,
				"to": 47360
			},
			"text": " A gamma ray is just what we call a very high-energy photon of electromagnetic radiation."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:47,360",
				"to": "00:00:50,580"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 47360,
				"to": 50580
			},
			"text": " When you see a chart of the electromagnetic spectrum, gamma rays are basically anything"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:50,580",
				"to": "00:00:52,140"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 50580,
				"to": 52140
			},
			"text": " more energetic than x-rays."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:52,140",
				"to": "00:00:54,060"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 52140,
				"to": 54060
			},
			"text": " At the high end, they're literally off the chart."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:54,060",
				"to": "00:00:56,860"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 54060,
				"to": 56860
			},
			"text": " They come from high-energy events like nuclear explosions."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:56,860",
				"to": "00:01:00,300"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 56860,
				"to": 60300
			},
			"text": " Gamma ray bursts are made when something very bad happens to a star."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:00,300",
				"to": "00:01:03,820"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 60300,
				"to": 63820
			},
			"text": " When massive stars collapse, their cores give in to the crushing pull of their own gravity,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:03,820",
				"to": "00:01:07,420"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 63820,
				"to": 67420
			},
			"text": " release an enormous burst of energy, and tear the star apart from the inside."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:07,420",
				"to": "00:01:10,700"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 67420,
				"to": 70700
			},
			"text": " For reasons that we don't fully understand, these explosions often produce jets shooting"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:10,700",
				"to": "00:01:13,080"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 70700,
				"to": 73080
			},
			"text": " away along the poles of the collapsing star."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:13,080",
				"to": "00:01:16,620"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 73080,
				"to": 76620
			},
			"text": " These jets can travel across much of the universe, and when Earth is in line with one of them,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:16,620",
				"to": "00:01:19,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 76620,
				"to": 79240
			},
			"text": " we see it as a flash of gamma rays from deep space."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:19,240",
				"to": "00:01:22,380"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 79240,
				"to": 82380
			},
			"text": " We didn't know about gamma ray bursts until we launched a satellite to watch for gamma"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:22,380",
				"to": "00:01:25,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 82380,
				"to": 85960
			},
			"text": " ray flashes from nuclear explosions on Earth, and we were surprised to see flashes coming"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:25,960",
				"to": "00:01:28,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 85960,
				"to": 88240
			},
			"text": " from everywhere else in the universe instead."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:28,240",
				"to": "00:01:32,220"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 88240,
				"to": 92220
			},
			"text": " The peak power of beams from gamma ray bursts can be on the order of 10^44 watts, which"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:32,220",
				"to": "00:01:34,940"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 92220,
				"to": 94940
			},
			"text": " is much, much more powerful than our laser array."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:34,940",
				"to": "00:01:38,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 94940,
				"to": 98880
			},
			"text": " To get a 10^44 watt death ray of our own, we'd need to give each person on the moon-facing"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:38,880",
				"to": "00:01:42,080"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 98880,
				"to": 102080
			},
			"text": " side of the planet a 2x10^34 watt laser."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:42,080",
				"to": "00:01:45,700"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 102080,
				"to": 105700
			},
			"text": " That is, each person would need a laser 10 billion times more powerful than the final"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:45,700",
				"to": "00:01:48,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 105700,
				"to": 108600
			},
			"text": " combined laser that violently ejected the moon."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:48,600",
				"to": "00:01:52,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 108600,
				"to": 112600
			},
			"text": " This is an implausible scenario, and it wouldn't work for reasons we'll get to in a minute."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:52,600",
				"to": "00:01:55,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 112600,
				"to": 115200
			},
			"text": " But first, let's think about what we could do with a beam like that."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:55,200",
				"to": "00:01:58,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 115200,
				"to": 118460
			},
			"text": " We'd have to focus it carefully, since laser beams spread out as they travel."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:58,460",
				"to": "00:02:01,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 118460,
				"to": 121520
			},
			"text": " The minimum angle of spread depends on the size of the source of the beam."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:01,520",
				"to": "00:02:05,640"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 121520,
				"to": 125640
			},
			"text": " For laser beams emitted by lenses 2 meters wide, the limit is about 0.1 arc seconds,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:05,640",
				"to": "00:02:07,620"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 125640,
				"to": 127620
			},
			"text": " or 3/100 thousandths of a degree."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:07,620",
				"to": "00:02:11,560"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 127620,
				"to": 131560
			},
			"text": " The laser beam limit formula is weirdly similar to the formula used to determine the maximum"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:11,560",
				"to": "00:02:15,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 131560,
				"to": 135600
			},
			"text": " resolution of telescopes like Hubble, because in a sense, a telescope is just a death ray"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:15,600",
				"to": "00:02:16,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 135600,
				"to": 136600
			},
			"text": " running in reverse."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:16,600",
				"to": "00:02:21,600"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 136600,
				"to": 141600
			},
			"text": " Hubble has a 2.4 meter mirror, and its angular resolution is a little less than 0.1 arc seconds,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:21,600",
				"to": "00:02:24,040"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 141600,
				"to": 144040
			},
			"text": " similar to the angular limit of our 2 meter laser."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:24,040",
				"to": "00:02:27,920"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 144040,
				"to": 147920
			},
			"text": " The laser array from the original chapter was pretty powerful but not particularly narrow."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:27,920",
				"to": "00:02:31,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 147920,
				"to": 151520
			},
			"text": " If it had been focused into a Hubble-style beam, it could conceivably have fried the"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:31,520",
				"to": "00:02:33,920"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 151520,
				"to": 153920
			},
			"text": " surfaces of planets anywhere in our galaxy."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:33,920",
				"to": "00:02:37,000"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 153920,
				"to": 157000
			},
			"text": " A 10^44 watt death ray would be much worse."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:37,000",
				"to": "00:02:40,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 157000,
				"to": 160680
			},
			"text": " If we tightly focused it down to the diffraction limit, it could reach targets far outside"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:40,680",
				"to": "00:02:45,140"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 160680,
				"to": 165140
			},
			"text": " our galaxy, frying the surfaces of planets up to 5 or 10 billion light years away."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:45,140",
				"to": "00:02:48,560"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 165140,
				"to": 168560
			},
			"text": " But don't rush out to buy a 10^44 watt laser just yet."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:48,560",
				"to": "00:02:51,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 168560,
				"to": 171760
			},
			"text": " At cosmic energy scales, normal optics breaks down."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:51,760",
				"to": "00:02:56,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 171760,
				"to": 176480
			},
			"text": " For example, if a beam is powerful enough, it could exert a gravitational pull on itself."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:56,480",
				"to": "00:02:59,260"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 176480,
				"to": 179260
			},
			"text": " Photons carry energy, and energy creates gravitational fields."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:59,260",
				"to": "00:03:03,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 179260,
				"to": 183400
			},
			"text": " For normal light beams, this is negligible, but for a 10^44 watt laser the size of the"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:03,400",
				"to": "00:03:07,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 183400,
				"to": 187440
			},
			"text": " Earth, photons on the outer edge would experience an acceleration of over 10 g's toward the"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:07,440",
				"to": "00:03:08,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 187440,
				"to": 188840
			},
			"text": " beam's center line."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:08,840",
				"to": "00:03:12,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 188840,
				"to": 192880
			},
			"text": " But physics has another surprise, one that finally puts an upper limit on how powerful"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:12,880",
				"to": "00:03:13,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 192880,
				"to": 193960
			},
			"text": " lasers can get."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:13,960",
				"to": "00:03:18,640"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 193960,
				"to": 198640
			},
			"text": " Namely, if a beam of light gets too bright, space itself stops being transparent."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:18,640",
				"to": "00:03:21,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 198640,
				"to": 201960
			},
			"text": " If you pack enough laser energy into a small enough space, quantum mechanics predicts that"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:21,960",
				"to": "00:03:26,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 201960,
				"to": 206720
			},
			"text": " the strong electromagnetic fields will result in spontaneous creation of particles and antiparticles."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:26,720",
				"to": "00:03:30,800"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 206720,
				"to": 210800
			},
			"text": " These particles, mostly electrons and positrons, would intercept some of the laser energy, which"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:30,800",
				"to": "00:03:32,900"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 210800,
				"to": 212900
			},
			"text": " would result in more particles being created."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:32,900",
				"to": "00:03:37,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 212900,
				"to": 217200
			},
			"text": " For laser power densities above about 10^26 watts per square centimeter, this process is"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:37,200",
				"to": "00:03:41,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 217200,
				"to": 221720
			},
			"text": " expected to cascade, fully halting the laser's progress and providing an upper limit on how"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:41,720",
				"to": "00:03:43,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 221720,
				"to": 223520
			},
			"text": " much power our beam can have."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:03:43,520",
				"to": "00:03:46,300"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 223520,
				"to": 226300
			},
			"text": " In the end, it turns out, physics is not math."
		},
		{
